                <pb facs="0494" n="453" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve15p2/pg453"/>

                <head>129. National Security Study Memorandum 189<anchor n="1" xml:id="d129-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1973-11-14"
                        >November 14, 1973</date>.</dateline>
                <list type="description">
                    <label>TO</label>
                    <item>The Secretary of State</item>
                    <item>The Secretary of Defense</item>
                    <item>Chairman, NSC Under Secretaries
                        Committee</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Azores Base Agreement Negotiations</item>
                </list>
                <p>The President has directed that the NSC Under
                    Secretaries Committee undertake a priority review of the U.S.-Portuguese Azores
                    base negotiations. The study should identify the U.S. interests involved in the
                    base negotiations as well as recommendations for the U.S. position <pb
                        facs="0495" n="454" xml:id="pg454"/> best suited to protect those interests,
                    taking into account such factors as:</p>
                <p>—the overall status of U.S.-Portuguese relations;</p>
                <p>—the present and future strategic importance of the Azores/Lajes facilities;</p>
                <p>—the best U.S. estimate of the Portuguese position in the negotiations; and</p>
                <p>—Congressional considerations bearing on the recommended U.S. position.</p>
                <p>The Chairman, Under Secretaries Committee, is requested to forward the study
                    response no later than December 7, 1973, for consideration by the President.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed corresp="#p_KHA_1">
                        Henry A. Kissinger
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d129-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d129-f1-content">
                <seg type="summary">Summary: The President directed a priority review of the
                    U.S.-Portuguese Azores Base negotiations.</seg>
                <p><seg type="source">Source: National Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials,
                            NSC Files, NSC Institutional Files (H-Files), Box H–201, Study
                        Memorandums, 1969–1974, NSSM–189.
                        Confidential. Copies were sent to the DCI
                        and the Chairman of the JCS. Scowcroft signed the memorandum on
                            Kissinger’s behalf. In a
                        November 6 memorandum to Kissinger
                        on the Azores Base agreement negotiations, Sonnenfeldt wrote that the use of the Azores Base during the
                        Middle East crisis had changed the proposed U.S. negotiating position that
                        “mutually beneficial cooperation between two members of the NATO Alliance should not involve
                        compensation.” Rush now wanted an
                        interagency review of the U.S. position; Sonnenfeldt agreed that it was necessary because “the
                        Portuguese can be expected to ask for compensation for future use of the
                        Lajes facilities, and accordingly it is important that a coordinated
                        State/Defense position for the negotiations be developed within the NSC system.” (Ibid.)</seg></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
